  "system_prompt": "You are a computational chemist designing focused compound libraries. Always respond with valid JSON containing a 'modifications' list with exactly 5 entries. Each modification must include 'description', 'smiles', and 'rationale' fields.",
  "user_prompt": "Design a focused analog library of 5 compounds based on Remdesivir (SMILES: CCC(CC)COC(=O)[C@@H](N[P@@](=O)(OCC1C(O)C(O)C(n2cnc3c(N)ncnc23)O1)Oc1ccccc1)C) with systematic modifications at key positions to explore SAR against SARS-CoV-2 RdRp. Include SMILES for each analog.\n\nRespond ONLY with JSON in this exact format:\n{\"modifications\": [{\"description\": \"analog 1 description\", \"smiles\": \"SMILES_1\", \"rationale\": \"rationale 1\"}, {\"description\": \"analog 2 description\", \"smiles\": \"SMILES_2\", \"rationale\": \"rationale 2\"}, {\"description\": \"analog 3 description\", \"smiles\": \"SMILES_3\", \"rationale\": \"rationale 3\"}, {\"description\": \"analog 4 description\", \"smiles\": \"SMILES_4\", \"rationale\": \"rationale 4\"}, {\"description\": \"analog 5 description\", \"smiles\": \"SMILES_5\", \"rationale\": \"rationale 5\"}]}",
  "raw_response": "```json\n{\n  \"modifications\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Replace the isopropyl group with a cyclopropyl group to investigate steric effects on binding.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"C1CC1COC(=O)[C@@H](N[P@@](=O)(OCC1C(O)C(O)C(n2cnc3c(N)ncnc23)O1)Oc1ccccc1)C\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Cyclopropyl substitution may enhance binding affinity by altering the spatial fit within the active site of RdRp.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Introduce a fluorine atom on the benzyl ether to explore electronic effects on interactions with the RdRp binding site.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"CCC(CC)COC(=O)[C@@H](N[P@@](=O)(OCC1C(O)C(O)C(n2cnc3c(N)ncnc23)O1)Oc1ccc(F)cc1)C\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Fluorination can modulate hydrogen bonding and lipophilicity, potentially improving binding efficiency.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Add a methyl group to the ribose 5'-hydroxyl group to study steric hindrance effects.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"CCC(CC)COC(=O)[C@@H](N[P@@](=O)(OCC1C(O)C(O)C(n2cnc3c(N)ncnc23)OC1)Oc1ccccc1)C\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Methylation could influence the positioning of the ribose moiety within the RdRp active site and modify binding interactions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Replace the phenyl ring with a pyridyl ring to explore heteroaromatic interactions.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"CCC(CC)COC(=O)[C@@H](N[P@@](=O)(OCC1C(O)C(O)C(n2cnc3c(N)ncnc23)O1)Oc1ccncc1)C\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The nitrogen in the pyridyl ring may form additional hydrogen bonds or alter the electronic distribution in the binding pocket.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Substitute the nitrile group in the nucleobase with an amino group to assess changes in hydrogen bonding with RdRp.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"CCC(CC)COC(=O)[C@@H](N[P@@](=O)(OCC1C(O)C(O)C(n2cnc3c(N)cnc23)O1)Oc1ccccc1)C\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Replacing the nitrile group with an amino group could enhance interactions with hydrogen-bond donors or acceptors in the RdRp active site.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
